{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-cc482d12-d7db-441a-870d-6a8d3235845b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8d8124b23b9501a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-8nh9oix9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E002.md","content":"# Investigate artifact path workspace-context resolvability and enforcement completeness\n\n## Description\n\nResolve whether artifact requests in the artifacts-only server carry enough information to resolve\nworkspace membership, and whether the planned workspace validation closes every failure and bypass\nmode. The strategy flags the assumption \"artifact request paths in the `/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*`\nendpoints include sufficient information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace membership\"\nas needing validation, and its risks identify artifact path resolution complexity and the possibility\nof artifact requests bypassing workspace validation. Because this strategy adds new authorization\nenforcement (tenant isolation with fail-closed denial), this investigation provides the combined\nfail-mode and security analysis that gates the server implementation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Determine, for the S3 artifact store configuration (the standard RHOAI configuration, where\n  artifact paths follow `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), whether every artifact request path\n  resolves to a parent experiment and thus to a workspace assignment.\n- Identify artifact request shapes that cannot be resolved (non-standard artifact roots, custom\n  artifact root configurations, malformed paths) and confirm each is denied under the fail-closed\n  design rather than served.\n- Enumerate failure modes of the validation path — workspace store unreachable, workspace store\n  error versus definitive non-membership, auth plugin failure, invalid or missing workspace\n  context — and verify the fail-closed design (deny, never serve without validation) covers each.\n- Identify bypass vectors for workspace validation in artifact serving (path forms that evade\n  experiment resolution, request paths that skip validation) and classify each as covered, denied by\n  design, or requiring remediation.\n- Produce recommendations that fix the resolution and validation approach for the workspace-aware\n  artifacts-only server, including any remediation work discovered.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A findings document answers, with path-structure and code evidence, whether S3 artifact request\n  paths carry sufficient information to resolve workspace membership, and specifies the resolution\n  rule the server implementation should apply.\n- Every enumerated failure mode and bypass vector is classified as deny-by-design (fail-closed),\n  covered by existing validation, or flagged with concrete remediation for the workspace-aware\n  artifacts-only serving implementation.\n- No mode is left classified as \"serve without validation\"; any uncovered mode is escalated as\n  remediation scope for the workspace-aware artifacts-only serving implementation.\n- Documented limitations for non-standard artifact roots are drafted (per the strategy's risk\n  mitigation) so the server implementation can include them.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Validates the assumption gating the HLR \"`--artifacts-only` can be combined with\n  `--enable-workspaces` ...\" (P0) and the HLR \"Artifact requests ... are validated against workspace\n  membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403\" (P0).\n- Verifies fail-closed coverage for the HLR \"Workspace-aware artifact serving is fail-closed: if the\n  workspace store is unreachable, requests are denied\" (P0) and the Security NFR (\"Requests with\n  invalid or missing workspace context are denied, not served\").\n- Addresses the strategy risks \"Artifact path resolution complexity\" and \"Split-deployment\n  operational complexity\" (bypass via misconfiguration).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":68579,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88a7f54f0bdff0ba","agent_id":"ac3ea9291bd90e561","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"782ac07e-531d-4c48-9af0-8dbf90afb47e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:20:05.723Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
