{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4b2f92a0-ef83-42b7-817e-934fdfe9e197","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cfdb0dd25035a2e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-8nh9oix9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n\n## Description\n\nDecide how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking\ndeployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The strategy flags\nthis as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: the answer \"affects HTTPRoute design and\ndetermines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact\noperations\". The answer selects between two bounded outcomes and sets the routing scope of the\noperator's split-server implementation, adding server-side delegation work in one outcome.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Analyze the operator's existing Gateway API routing pattern (conditional HTTPRoute creation via\n  runtime CRD discovery) for its applicability to routing artifact traffic to a dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance.\n- Determine whether HTTPRoute-based routing alone can direct artifact API traffic from the main\n  tracking deployment's route to the artifacts-only instance's Service.\n- Determine whether the tracking server instead needs a configuration change to delegate artifact\n  operations to the dedicated instance (for example, an upstream or proxy configuration on the main\n  tracking deployment).\n- Assess backwards-compatibility impact: deployments not using split-server artifact serving must\n  reconcile unchanged.\n- Record the bounded outcome: (A) HTTPRoute-only routing suffices, or (B) tracking server\n  configuration change required, with the design each outcome implies.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A design document selects the routing mechanism with rationale grounded in the operator's existing\n  Helm-in-operator and conditional CRD discovery patterns, and states which bounded outcome holds.\n- For the selected outcome, the design specifies what the operator renders and configures for\n  artifact traffic routing, sufficient to set the scope of the split-server operator implementation\n  without further design work.\n- If outcome B holds, the design specifies the tracking-server-side configuration change needed to\n  delegate artifact operations, sufficient to scope a server-side delegation implementation.\n- The design confirms that deployments not opting into split-server artifact serving are unaffected.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Resolves the open question gating the HLR \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n  dedicated artifacts-only instance\" (P1) and informing the HLR \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\" (P1).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70192,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88a7f54f0bdff0ba","agent_id":"ac3ea9291bd90e561","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"61d46199-2bc7-48cc-898c-36d348b8c656","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:20:14.444Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
