{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90cffde5f4217a2a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate workspace provider initialization coupling in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate workspace provider initialization coupling in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve whether the Kubernetes workspace provider in the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` package can\n30\tinitialize and resolve experiment-to-workspace mapping in a server context where the tracking store\n31\tand model registry store are not initialized. The strategy flags this both as an open question\n32\t(\"Does the workspace store initialization in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins depend on tracking store\n33\tavailability?\") and as an assumption needing validation (\"the workspace store provides\n34\texperiment-to-workspace mapping that is accessible without initializing tracking stores\"). The\n35\tanswer determines whether the plugin's workspace resolution must be refactored into an independent\n36\tinitialization path before it can back workspace-aware artifacts-only serving.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Trace the plugin's initialization dependency chain: registration through the\n41\t  `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group, loading via `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`, and\n42\t  `kubernetes://` workspace store resolution.\n43\t- Determine definitively whether any part of that chain requires tracking store or model registry\n44\t  store initialization.\n45\t- If coupled: produce a refactoring plan that factors workspace resolution into an independent\n46\t  initialization path within the plugin, preserving the existing entry-point interface and the\n47\t  plugin's behavior for the tracking server's non-artifact operations.\n48\t- If not coupled: produce verification evidence (for example, a reproducible test exercising\n49\t  experiment-to-workspace resolution with tracking stores uninitialized).\n50\t- Record the bounded outcome (coupled / not coupled) and the resulting scope for the plugin\n51\t  extension work.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A findings document states, with code references, whether the workspace provider's initialization\n56\t  and resolution path depends on tracking store or model registry store availability, and identifies\n57\t  the exact coupling points if it does.\n58\t- If coupled, the refactoring plan scopes the independent initialization path, lists the affected\n59\t  plugin modules, and confirms the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point interface is preserved.\n60\t- If not coupled, a reproducible verification demonstrates experiment-to-workspace resolution\n61\t  succeeding with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n62\t- The outcome is recorded as one of the two bounded answers and is sufficient to set the scope of\n63\t  the downstream plugin extension work without further analysis.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- Resolves the open question and assumption gating the HLR \"Auth plugin workspace resolution\n68\t  functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization\" (P1) and,\n69\t  through it, the HLR \"Artifact requests ... are validated against workspace membership\" (P0).\n70\t- Addresses the strategy risk \"Auth plugin coupling to full server initialization\" (validate the\n71\t  plugin's initialization dependencies early, per the strategy's mitigation).\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d0bd6bd2abb5543","agent_id":"a0d0c460e417dbaec","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"24b08cba-04d2-4f86-9ab6-049e175b6a10","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:23:05.213Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90cffde5f4217a2a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
