{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bedfe7bdcada0be","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Extend mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the workspace provider's initialization is coupled to tracking\n16\t    store availability, this epic's scope expands to refactor workspace resolution\n17\t    into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving the entry-point\n18\t    interface.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 0\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Extend mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only context\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tVerify and extend the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin so workspace resolution functions\n41\tcorrectly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are\n42\tnot initialized. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking\n43\tserver's non-artifact operations through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group; this\n44\tepic ensures the same resolution works when only the workspace provider is initialized. The\n45\tauthentication layer is unchanged: the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth`\n46\tsetup work identically for the artifacts-only instance and the main tracking server (Staff Engineer\n47\tinput).\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Verify workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace mapping via the `kubernetes://` workspace\n52\t  store) in a server context with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n53\t- If the workspace provider's initialization is found to be coupled to tracking store availability\n54\t  (per the findings of the workspace provider initialization investigation): refactor workspace\n55\t  resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving the\n56\t  `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point interface and `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` loading.\n57\t- Extend the plugin as needed so artifact request paths can be resolved to workspace membership\n58\t  through the same resolution logic the tracking server uses for non-artifact operations.\n59\t- Preserve existing behavior for the tracking server's non-artifact workspace operations (no\n60\t  regression).\n61\t- Do not change the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar or `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Workspace resolution returns the correct experiment-to-workspace mapping in the artifacts-only\n66\t  context, demonstrated with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n67\t- If refactoring was required: workspace resolution initializes through an independent path, the\n68\t  `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point interface is unchanged, and the plugin still loads via\n69\t  `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`.\n70\t- The plugin's behavior for the tracking server's existing non-artifact workspace operations is\n71\t  unchanged (regression tests pass).\n72\t- The authentication setup (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) requires no\n73\t  changes and works identically for the artifacts-only instance.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- P1 HLR, inheriting P0 through enablement: Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in\n78\t  the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — this capability enables the P0\n79\t  workspace-membership validation of artifact requests.\n80\t- Addresses the strategy dependency \"mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin (internal, exists): may\n81\t  require extension if workspace resolution is currently coupled to the full tracking server\n82\t  initialization path\" and the risk \"Auth plugin coupling to full server initialization\".\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d0bd6bd2abb5543","agent_id":"a0d0c460e417dbaec","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"7bc32eba-ed8d-443c-9dc3-a02cf7319c96","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:23:10.551Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bedfe7bdcada0be","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
