{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e00258597895dba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator split-server topology for a dedicated artifacts-only instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design selects tracking-server-side delegation\n15\t    instead of HTTPRoute-only routing, this epic's routing configuration and main-deployment\n16\t    template scope change accordingly.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 5\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# MLflow operator split-server topology for a dedicated artifacts-only instance\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate\n39\tDeployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, and to configure the main tracking deployment to\n40\troute artifact traffic to that instance — a split-server topology, not a single-deployment\n41\tconfiguration toggle (Staff Engineer input). The operator continues to use its Helm-in-operator\n42\tpattern: the MLflow CR spec is converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates,\n43\tand applied via Server-Side Apply, with Gateway API HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based\n44\ton runtime CRD discovery.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, separate from\n49\t  the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n50\t- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`,\n51\t  `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration\n52\t  mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment.\n53\t- Configuration of artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated\n54\t  artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism selected by the artifact traffic routing design\n55\t  investigation (HTTPRoute-based routing, or routing that relies on a tracking-server-side\n56\t  delegation configuration if that outcome holds).\n57\t- Declarative CR surface: users configure a single MLflow CR for the split topology rather than\n58\t  managing individual resources.\n59\t- Operator validation that rejects split-serving configurations where the artifacts-only instance\n60\t  lacks workspace flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation —\n61\t  strategy risk mitigation).\n62\t- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking\n63\t  deployment (passive component: the authentication layer is unchanged).\n64\t- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs not using split-server artifact serving reconcile exactly as\n65\t  before.\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated\n70\t  artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment —\n71\t  measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n72\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces\n73\t  --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by\n74\t  inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n75\t- The MLflow image deployed to the artifacts-only instance supports the combined\n76\t  `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces` serving mode (configuration reference gate — the image\n77\t  reference is resolved at deployment time, not a build-time dependency).\n78\t- Artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only\n79\t  instance is configured per the selected routing design.\n80\t- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created conditionally based on runtime CRD\n81\t  discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n82\t- The operator rejects split-serving configurations whose artifacts-only instance lacks workspace\n83\t  flags, with a clear status condition.\n84\t- The artifacts-only Deployment includes the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar configured identically to the\n85\t  main tracking deployment.\n86\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile with no changes to previously rendered\n87\t  resources (backwards compatibility).\n88\t- The split topology is expressed declaratively through a single MLflow CR.\n89\t\n90\t## HLR Traceability\n91\t\n92\t- P1: MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its\n93\t  own Service and HTTPRoute.\n94\t- P1: Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n95\t- P0 (regression share): Single-tenant deployments and configurations without `--enable-workspaces`\n96\t  retain current behavior with no changes.\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d0bd6bd2abb5543","agent_id":"a0d0c460e417dbaec","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"b0e264bc-d3cd-4c26-a3e9-9c3e0b0a24cb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:23:11.148Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e00258597895dba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
