gation, sidecar, validation, backwards compat) and (b) artifact\ntraffic routing from the main tracking deployment — the E003-gated part that pairs with\nBRANCH-B-E007 under outcome B. E004 (strategy estimate 1-2 sprints, plus audit logging,\ncaching, and limitations documentation) is borderline and should be re-checked after the E006\nsplit, but is not itself a violation at the low end of its estimate.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\nAll three Investigations genuinely change downstream structure: E001's outcome rewrites E005's\nscope (verify vs. refactor), E002's outcome rewrites E004's resolution/validation approach,\nE003's outcome selects E006's routing scope and whether BRANCH-B-E007 exists at all. All\nImplementations produce concrete artifacts. Gating metadata is complete and correct: every\ngated epic has `gated_by` set to an Investigation that appears in its direct `dependencies`,\nand every `gate_failure_impact` has both `action` and a substantive `fallback_approach`\n(rewrite for E004/E005/E006; remove for the branch epic, correctly reflecting outcome A).\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\nType-appropriate signal sets are used throughout (investigation_signals on E001-E003,\nai_signals on the four Implementations); no epic mixes sets, and all seven rationale files\nexist. Signal values are consistent with rubric conditions and strategy content, including the\nhonest negatives (E005 repo_access=0 with unconfirmed plugin repo, matching Health Warning 3;\nE004/E005/E006 open_questions=-1 reflecting their gates). One arguable mis-score:\nBRANCH-B-E007 sets `pattern_precedent: 0` while its own rationale states the rubric's -1\ncondition verbatim (\"The tracking server has no existing mechanism for delegating artifact\noperations to another instance\"); `change_specificity: 0` is similarly arguable for -1 given\nthe delegation mechanism is unknown until E003 resolves. One-to-two arguable values → 1 point,\nnot a rubric contradiction.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs. All six strategy acceptance criteria are carried: ACs 1-4 into\nE004 (200/403/503, fail-closed, missing-store-uri startup failure, combined-mode store\ninitialization), ACs 5-6 into E006 (distinct Deployment resources; exact container command\nflags). Backwards-compatibility ACs are present on E004, E006, and BRANCH-B-E007\n(configuration-absent behavior preserved). No soft ACs misfile external schedule constraints;\nthe latency AC (\"measured and reported\", short-TTL caching implemented) is testable. No epic\nbody references siblings by draft ID — investigations are referenced by title. konflux and\ndocs-authoring rule-mandated ACs are N/A (no such epics).\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nThe combined epic set covers all three affected components and every strategy capability:\nflag composition, workspace validation with fail-closed denial, plugin resolution in the\nartifacts-only context, split-server operator topology, artifact traffic routing (both\nbounded outcomes), audit logging, and non-standard-artifact-root documentation. Strategy\nrisks are carried forward (path-resolution complexity → E002; plugin coupling → E001/E005;\nsplit-topology misconfiguration → E006's rejection validation; per-request latency → E004's\ncaching AC and Health Warning 2), as are the \"needs validation\" assumptions and the open\nquestions (with Rule 4 reclassifications documented in the summary). NFRs map to ACs (Security\nfail-closed, Backwards Compatibility, Performance). Out-of-scope items are respected. The\nconditional branch covers both stated outcomes of the routing question (A: E006 alone; B:\nBRANCH-B-E007). Docs-authoring epic not required: the strategy's Documentation Support gate is\n\"Pending human review\", not \"Yes\".\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50043,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d0bd6