{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af924f0064aa9a1e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDecide how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking\n30\tdeployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The strategy flags\n31\tthis as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: the answer \"affects HTTPRoute design and\n32\tdetermines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact\n33\toperations\". The answer selects between two bounded outcomes and sets the routing scope of the\n34\toperator's split-server implementation, adding server-side delegation work in one outcome.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Analyze the operator's existing Gateway API routing pattern (conditional HTTPRoute creation via\n39\t  runtime CRD discovery) for its applicability to routing artifact traffic to a dedicated\n40\t  artifacts-only instance.\n41\t- Determine whether HTTPRoute-based routing alone can direct artifact API traffic from the main\n42\t  tracking deployment's route to the artifacts-only instance's Service.\n43\t- Determine whether the tracking server instead needs a configuration change to delegate artifact\n44\t  operations to the dedicated instance (for example, an upstream or proxy configuration on the main\n45\t  tracking deployment).\n46\t- Assess backwards-compatibility impact: deployments not using split-server artifact serving must\n47\t  reconcile unchanged.\n48\t- Record the bounded outcome: (A) HTTPRoute-only routing suffices, or (B) tracking server\n49\t  configuration change required, with the design each outcome implies.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A design document selects the routing mechanism with rationale grounded in the operator's existing\n54\t  Helm-in-operator and conditional CRD discovery patterns, and states which bounded outcome holds.\n55\t- For the selected outcome, the design specifies what the operator renders and configures for\n56\t  artifact traffic routing, sufficient to set the scope of the split-server operator implementation\n57\t  without further design work.\n58\t- If outcome B holds, the design specifies the tracking-server-side configuration change needed to\n59\t  delegate artifact operations, sufficient to scope a server-side delegation implementation.\n60\t- The design confirms that deployments not opting into split-server artifact serving are unaffected.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- Resolves the open question gating the HLR \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n65\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance\" (P1) and informing the HLR \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated\n66\t  artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\" (P1).\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b29c130e8383fd1f","agent_id":"a01af53f7393d48ff","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"0ad27d51-85aa-452a-8345-23038f403586","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:28:32.100Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af924f0064aa9a1e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type"