{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89f076c402d7c1c4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E007\n3\ttitle: Tracking server artifact traffic delegation configuration (branch B)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: 'If HTTPRoute-only routing suffices (outcome A), no tracking-server\n16\t    delegation change is needed: artifact traffic is routed entirely via Gateway API\n17\t    HTTPRoute rules and this epic is dropped.'\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Tracking server artifact traffic delegation configuration (branch B)\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplement the tracking-server-side configuration change that delegates artifact operations to the\n39\tdedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. This epic exists only if the\n40\tartifact traffic routing design investigation resolves to the outcome where HTTPRoute-based routing\n41\talone is insufficient and the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact\n42\toperations. If HTTPRoute-only routing suffices, this epic is not needed.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Implement the tracking server configuration mechanism that routes and delegates artifact\n47\t  operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the selected routing design.\n48\t- Ensure the configuration is settable through the mechanisms the MLflow operator already uses to\n49\t  configure the main tracking deployment, so the operator can propagate it declaratively from the\n50\t  MLflow CR.\n51\t- Preserve current behavior when the delegation configuration is absent: the main tracking server\n52\t  continues to serve artifacts itself.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- With the delegation configuration set, artifact requests to the main tracking server are routed\n57\t  to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (measured by artifact responses originating from the\n58\t  artifacts-only instance).\n59\t- Without the delegation configuration, the main tracking server serves artifacts itself — current\n60\t  behavior preserved (backwards compatibility).\n61\t- The configuration can be propagated by the MLflow operator through its existing configuration\n62\t  mechanisms for the main tracking deployment.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- P1 (branch-B share, alongside the operator's split-server topology implementation): Main tracking\n67\t  deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b29c130e8383fd1f","agent_id":"a01af53f7393d48ff","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"88cb82e6-2a82-46bd-aaaa-48946149debd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:28:32.705Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89f076c402d7c1c4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
