ment through the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main\n  tracking deployment, so it can be set declaratively from the MLflow CR.\n- Keep routing configuration conditional: MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving render\n  no routing changes.\n- Backwards compatibility: without routing configuration, the main tracking deployment continues\n  to serve artifacts itself.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment is routed to the dedicated artifacts-only\n  instance per the selected routing design — measured by artifact requests against the main\n  deployment being served by the artifacts-only instance.\n- Under the HTTPRoute-only outcome, Gateway API routing rules direct artifact API traffic to the\n  artifacts-only instance's Service, created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery,\n  consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n- Under the delegation outcome, the delegation configuration is propagated to the main tracking\n  deployment through the operator's existing configuration mechanisms and is settable from the\n  MLflow CR.\n- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving render no routing configuration and reconcile\n  with no changes to previously rendered resources (backwards compatibility).\n- Without routing configuration, the main tracking deployment serves artifacts itself — current\n  behavior preserved.\n- The routing configuration is expressed declaratively through the single MLflow CR (no manual\n  resource management).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P1: Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n- P0 (regression share): Single-tenant deployments and configurations without `--enable-workspaces`\n  retain current behavior with no changes.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49647,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null}