{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b0b3b62c-2139-4dfd-82f0-7208f4845a66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9c59cbf83c8b3d1","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-8nh9oix9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E006.md","old_string":"# MLflow operator split-server topology for a dedicated artifacts-only instance\n\n## Description\n\nExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate\nDeployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, and to configure the main tracking deployment to\nroute artifact traffic to that instance — a split-server topology, not a single-deployment\nconfiguration toggle (Staff Engineer input). The operator continues to use its Helm-in-operator\npattern: the MLflow CR spec is converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates,\nand applied via Server-Side Apply, with Gateway API HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based\non runtime CRD discovery.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, separate from\n  the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`,\n  `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration\n  mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment.\n- Configuration of artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism selected by the artifact traffic routing design\n  investigation (HTTPRoute-based routing, or routing that relies on a tracking-server-side\n  delegation configuration if that outcome holds).\n- Declarative CR surface: users configure a single MLflow CR for the split topology rather than\n  managing individual resources.\n- Operator validation that rejects split-serving configurations where the artifacts-only instance\n  lacks workspace flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation —\n  strategy risk mitigation).\n- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking\n  deployment (passive component: the authentication layer is unchanged).\n- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs not using split-server artifact serving reconcile exactly as\n  before.","new_string":"# MLflow operator deployment of a dedicated artifacts-only instance\n\n## Description\n\nExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate\nDeployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — the instance-deployment half of the split-server\ntopology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff Engineer input). Configuring artifact\ntraffic routing from the main tracking deployment to that instance is carried by a separate epic.\nThe operator continues to use its Helm-in-operator pattern: the MLflow CR spec is converted to Helm\nvalues, rendered through embedded chart templates, and applied via Server-Side Apply, with Gateway\nAPI HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, separate from\n  the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`,\n  `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration\n  mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment.\n- Declarative CR surface: users configure a single MLflow CR for the split topology rather than\n  managing individual resources.\n- Operator validation that rejects split-serving configurations where the artifacts-only instance\n  lacks workspace flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation —\n  strategy risk mitigation).\n- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking\n  deployment (passive component: the authentication layer is unchanged).\n- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs not using split-server artifact serving reconcile exactly as\n  before."}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52802,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b29c130e8383fd1f","agent_id":"a01af53f7393d48ff","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"e5e51ec2-699a-4ce3-8229-61c771274cfb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:33:12.247Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
