{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d99378c8b5ecaa9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator deployment of a dedicated artifacts-only instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design selects tracking-server-side delegation\n15\t    instead of HTTPRoute-only routing, the artifacts-only instance's HTTPRoute design\n16\t    may change; the deployment templates, workspace flag propagation, sidecar, and\n17\t    validation scope are unaffected.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# MLflow operator deployment of a dedicated artifacts-only instance\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate\n40\tDeployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — the instance-deployment half of the split-server\n41\ttopology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff Engineer input). Configuring artifact\n42\ttraffic routing from the main tracking deployment to that instance is carried by a separate epic.\n43\tThe operator continues to use its Helm-in-operator pattern: the MLflow CR spec is converted to Helm\n44\tvalues, rendered through embedded chart templates, and applied via Server-Side Apply, with Gateway\n45\tAPI HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, separate from\n50\t  the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n51\t- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`,\n52\t  `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration\n53\t  mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment.\n54\t- Declarative CR surface: users configure a single MLflow CR for the split topology rather than\n55\t  managing individual resources.\n56\t- Operator validation that rejects split-serving configurations where the artifacts-only instance\n57\t  lacks workspace flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation —\n58\t  strategy risk mitigation).\n59\t- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking\n60\t  deployment (passive component: the authentication layer is unchanged).\n61\t- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs not using split-server artifact serving reconcile exactly as\n62\t  before.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated\n67\t  artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment —\n68\t  measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n69\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces\n70\t  --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by\n71\t  inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n72\t- The MLflow image deployed to the artifacts-only instance supports the combined\n73\t  `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces` serving mode (configuration reference gate — the image\n74\t  reference is resolved at deployment time, not a build-time dependency).\n75\t- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created conditionally based on runtime CRD\n76\t  discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n77\t- The operator rejects split-serving configurations whose artifacts-only instance lacks workspace\n78\t  flags, with a clear status condition.\n79\t- The artifacts-only Deployment includes the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar configured identically to the\n80\t  main tracking deployment.\n81\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile with no changes to previously rendered\n82\t  resources (backwards compatibility).\n83\t- The split topology is expressed declaratively through a single MLflow CR.\n84\t\n85\t## HLR Traceability\n86\t\n87\t- P1: MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its\n88\t  own Service and HTTPRoute.\n89\t- P0 (regression share): Single-tenant deployments and configurations without `--enable-workspaces`\n90\t  retain current behavior with no changes.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3abadb3cf21788a","agent_id":"ac79b6f5c19b332c7","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"71c49dc2-1350-4bd9-a0ed-a52d20ca7c76","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:36:08.092Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d99378c8b5ecaa9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
