{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a24f3ecb9872571","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E008\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design selects tracking-server-side delegation\n15\t    instead of HTTPRoute-only routing, this epic renders the operator-side delegation\n16\t    configuration instead of HTTPRoute-based routing rules; the propagation mechanism\n17\t    and scope change accordingly.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t\n36\t# MLflow operator artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConfigure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only\n41\tinstance in the split-server topology. The mechanism is selected by the artifact traffic routing\n42\tdesign investigation: either Gateway API HTTPRoute rules direct artifact traffic to the dedicated\n43\tinstance's Service, or the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact\n44\toperations — in which case this epic implements the operator side of that delegation (propagating\n45\tthe delegation configuration to the main tracking deployment), while the tracking-server-side\n46\tdelegation mechanism itself is the conditional branch epic that exists only in that outcome. The\n47\toperator continues to use its Helm-in-operator pattern: routing configuration is rendered from the\n48\tMLflow CR through embedded chart templates and applied via Server-Side Apply, so the split topology\n49\tstays declarative — users configure a single MLflow CR rather than managing individual resources.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Render the artifact traffic routing configuration selected by the routing design investigation:\n54\t  Gateway API HTTPRoute rules directing artifact API traffic from the main tracking deployment's\n55\t  route to the dedicated artifacts-only instance's Service (HTTPRoute-only outcome), or the\n56\t  operator-side propagation of the tracking server's artifact-delegation configuration (outcome\n57\t  requiring a server-side change).\n58\t- Under the delegation outcome, propagate the delegation configuration to the main tracking\n59\t  deployment through the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main\n60\t  tracking deployment, so it can be set declaratively from the MLflow CR.\n61\t- Keep routing configuration conditional: MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving render\n62\t  no routing changes.\n63\t- Backwards compatibility: without routing configuration, the main tracking deployment continues\n64\t  to serve artifacts itself.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- Artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment is routed to the dedicated artifacts-only\n69\t  instance per the selected routing design — measured by artifact requests against the main\n70\t  deployment being served by the artifacts-only instance.\n71\t- Under the HTTPRoute-only outcome, Gateway API routing rules direct artifact API traffic to the\n72\t  artifacts-only instance's Service, created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery,\n73\t  consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n74\t- Under the delegation outcome, the delegation configuration is propagated to the main tracking\n75\t  deployment through the operator's existing configuration mechanisms and is settable from the\n76\t  MLflow CR.\n77\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving render no routing configuration and reconcile\n78\t  with no changes to previously rendered resources (backwards compatibility).\n79\t- Without routing configuration, the main tracking deployment serves artifacts itself — current\n80\t  behavior preserved.\n81\t- The routing configuration is expressed declaratively through the single MLflow CR (no manual\n82\t  resource management).\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability\n85\t\n86\t- P1: Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n87\t- P0 (regression share): Single-tenant deployments and configurations without `--enable-workspaces`\n88\t  retain current behavior with no changes.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3abadb3cf21788a","agent_id":"ac79b6f5c19b332c7","session_id":"7838be6a-6dd6-47c0-b294-a71fb9a59c49","uuid":"da4befa5-159f-48fb-9c8f-72f55273f295","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:36:11.657Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a24f3ecb9872571","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
